  "Question": "A rectangle has an area of 12. Which of the following correctly describes the functional relationship between its length y and width x?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(y=12x\\)",
    "B": "\\(y=x/12\\)",
    "C": "\\(y=12/x\\) (\\(x>0\\))",
    "D": "\\(y=12-x\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Area = length × width, so \\(xy=12\\). Therefore, \\(y=12/x\\), with width \\(x>0\\).",
